# $shortPath(pPath) -> the path as the fields and the log show it: Lib.Class, then the rest as given
#   $root.$libs.Executor.$objects.Tool.$methods.//$edit//  ->  Executor.Tool.$methods.//$edit//
# Four fronts are read: $root.$libs.Lib.$group.Class, $libs.Lib.$group.Class, Lib.$group.Class, Lib.Class.
# Only the front is shortened; the rest after the class is kept character for character.
# The short form is for DISPLAY: Omnis refuses Lib.Class in code (owner, 2026-09-26), so a
# path that goes into notation is taken from the reference ($fullname), never from the field.
# Comes back unchanged: a path that does not resolve (a typo stays visible, and blue), a
# front that is no library ($clib, $cinst ...), and a short form that resolves to anything else.
Set reference longRef to iTools.$pathToRefQuiet(pPath)
If isclear(longRef)
	Quit method pPath
End If
Calculate shortText as pPath
If left(shortText,6)='$libs.'
	Calculate shortText as con('$root.',shortText) ## $shortenClassPath strips $root.$libs. as one piece
End If
If left(shortText,1)='$'&left(shortText,12)<>'$root.$libs.'
	Quit method pPath ## not a library front: keep it
End If
Calculate shortText as iTools.$shortenClassPath(shortText)
Set reference shortRef to iTools.$pathToRefQuiet(shortText)
If isclear(shortRef)
	Quit method pPath
End If
If shortRef.$fullname<>longRef.$fullname
	Quit method pPath ## the short form names something else: keep what was given
End If
Quit method shortText